3c99a46c607859def831d9e3969ef851f7776724059fc61e4d0","source":"data/families.json"},"state":"producer-declared","value":{"rows":[{"label":"Power-saving bounds for halving pairs and level switches","statements":["HalvingLines"]}],"scope":"A halving pair in an even planar point set is a pair whose line leaves equally many remaining points on each side. The formalization proves that some absolute $\\varepsilon>0$ and $C$ bound the number of halving pairs by $Cn^{4/3-\\varepsilon}$ for every sufficiently large even $n$ and every $n$-point set with no three collinear. It also proves a bound of the same form for all level-switch counts under the additional generic-position assumptions in the statement. The constants are existential.","title":"Power savings for planar halving lines and <i>k</i>-sets","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/183.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"The k-set clause — O(n(k+1)^{1/3−ε₀}) strictly separable k-subsets for 1 ≤ k ≤ n/2 under no-three-collinear — is not stated. The only k-dependent statement is a k-uniform C·n^{4/3−ε} bound on level-switch counts, and it needs additional genericity hypotheses.","note":null,"reading":"reading:3d4fe9bb74fe3a38231bbc19","source_term":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","state":"narrower"},{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":"First half is stated: `∃ ε>0, C, n₀, ∀ even n ≥ n₀, ∀ P, GeneralPosition P → halvingCount P ≤ C * n^(4/3-ε)`. The k-set claim O(n(k+1)^{1/3-ε0}) for 1 <= k <= n/2 is NOT stated: the second conjunct only bounds `switchCount P k` (level-switch pairs) by `C * n^(4/3-ε)` uniformly in k, for the stronger hypothesis `Generic P` (distinct x-coordinates/slopes plus a segment-crossing condition), i.e. a weaker, k-independent bound on a different count (docs: 'a bound of the same form for all level-switch counts under the additional generic-position assumptions').","reading":"reading:12d1b4e201c2ffc5a56d1486","source_term":"partial","state":"part"}],"readings":["reading:3d4fe9bb74fe3a38231bbc19","reading:12d1b4e201c2ffc5a56d1486"],"state":"different-scope-descriptions"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750","repository":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine","source":"cert-machine","url":"https://carlostoledo.co/reports/openai-math.html"},"id":"reading:3d4fe9bb74fe3a38231bbc19","pair_review":false,"review_state":"outside-report","source":"cert-machine","source_term":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","source_value":{"code":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","confidence":"high","disagreement":null,"gap":"The k-set clause — O(n(k+1)^{1/3−ε₀}) strictly separable k-subsets for 1 ≤ k ≤ n/2 under no-three-collinear — is not stated. The only k-dependent statement is a k-uniform C·n^{4/3−ε} bound on level-switch counts, and it needs additional genericity hypotheses.","openai_note_on_gap":"silent — docs/183.md:9 says 'It also proves a bound of the same for